{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact clean pushed head 47191d5d131bde502ae9770337a383f41d0c91bc, covering all six artifacts with lane report 97e32506 first. The screenshots and sampled source support the main diagnosis: row/thread aggregation is unexplained, selection walks an undirected component, permanent labels obscure cards, and initial fit makes dense graphs unreadable. The proposed plan still needs the following bounded corrections before it is an implementable answer to Hugh's request.\n\n1. High priority — specify a readable focus/navigation state (note lines 428-430, 473-478, 636-643). Stepping currently preserves the unreadable fit scale. Even the proposed 900px-pane fit gives a 12px title only 4.56 screen pixels on Chess; Tailapp is smaller. A 900px pane also cannot be described as available height inside a 900px window without accounting for the header and controls. Define how a person initially finds/selects a card, obtains readable type, follows an edge and returns to the overview at a real viewport size. Define which predecessor/successor Left/Right selects at a branch, how alternatives remain reachable, and how cycles terminate or are traversed. The 9-thread cycle has no unique 'next'. Make the after mockup demonstrate those rules and selected long-edge/gutter routing; moving 27 edges into one narrow gutter alone does not demonstrate that overlapping paths can be followed.\n\n2. Correct the lineage/count semantics (lines 344-345, 364-375, 402-405, 573-581). A directed path and a weakly connected group are different: the proposed '1 chain' small example branches, so define the count as connected groups (with its edge policy) or stop calling it the number of directed chains. The small mockup has four other ancestors, one other descendant and the selected card: '5 before, 2 after, 0 both' is inconsistent with six emphasized cards. Exclude the selected node from before/after counts; likewise the dense mockup's two ancestors plus eight cycle peers and one continuation imply 10 before, 9 after, 8 both, plus selection. Walk a projected successor_request transfer in reverse when selecting its successor as well as forward from its predecessor; the current 'before' bullet omits it despite the chain definition. Pin these cases explicitly and keep supersede-act contributors excluded.\n\n3. Complete the context-restoration/keyboard design (lines 432-436). Lifting scale/offset into ListView alone cannot preserve them: OutcomeMap.tsx:71 unconditionally fits in a mount effect, so it overwrites restored state on return. Specify when fit occurs and when saved state wins, including population/repository changes and vanished selection. Moving the SVG after the cards also changes paint/hit order; retain card hit targets and edge accessibility explicitly rather than treating DOM order as the entire fix. Include a rendered return-from-detail test and pointer/keyboard checks.\n\n4. Repair evidence provenance and accuracy. inspect(97e32506) shows only promise d9300454 as a basis. Governing request and AGENTS require behavior documentation to rest on the measured implementation artifacts, not just its producing request/promise. Publish the successor note artifact on suitable live measured-source bases. The source formulas also show that the claimed 124px leftward curve excursion (lines 289-294 and mockups) is a control-point offset, not the curve's actual extent: direct evaluation of the unchanged same-column cubic gives about 20.075px beyond each side. Correct the quantitative claim. The private ui-evidence replay material is not in the six-file head; provide a stable/reproducible evidence location or small retained fixtures/scripts for the key counts, while distinguishing the synthetic two-row Tailapp replay from the actual zero-open screenshot.\n\n5. Simplify the deliverable. The exact note is 809 lines/6,458 words against a concise brief. The same three changes and gates recur in sections 4, 6 and 8. Keep one short decision/interaction specification with the two mockups and one validation table; move detailed measurements and source traces into clearly separated supporting evidence. Do not make the implementation sequence claim that an unresolved branch/focus design is merely two graph walks and one layout class.\n\nArchitecture: the exact head changes one design note and five images only; no runtime contract changes. Proposed presentation work belongs to layer 7 and may combine projected provenance/transfer fields, without asserting new workflow authority. Preserve that boundary and update the documented selection/interaction contract in its eventual implementing head. The missing behavior-artifact provenance above is an architectural review gate.\n\nSecurity: inspected the exact changed paths and all five images; no executable changes, secrets or authority mutation found. Screenshots expose local repo paths and public workroom identifiers/text as expected. Preserve bounded complete relations, exact contributor access and truthful omissions; navigation must not hide unfinished counted rows or reinterpret retirement as transfer. No unresolved code security defect is claimed in this documentation-only head.\n\nSimplification: removing permanent labels and reusing the complete table are sound. The current plan overstates how much readability follows from gutter routing and state lifting; resolving the small interaction contract and cutting repeated prose is required before approval.\n\nValidation: own clean detached checkout at exact head, origin branch agreement, six-path diff and diff check; inspected five images, sampled the count/collapse, SCC ordering, selection, geometry, mount effect, current architecture and original outcome-map design citations. Installed locked UI dependencies without scripts and ran the existing outcome-map tests: 19/19 passed. Direct source-geometry calculation reproduced the tiny proposed font and corrected curve extent. No remediation source was changed and no resident was restarted.\n","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:97e32506067c3b9289d29adde71768f971af8de3","head":"47191d5d131bde502ae9770337a383f41d0c91bc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8b071df23138b534693050d0e1e30c169e2acebc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8b071df23138b534693050d0e1e30c169e2acebc","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}